    "kernel_output": {
      "type": "value",
      "data": {
        "done": true,
        "solids": 2,
        "volume": 7999.999999999999,
        "smallSolidVolume": 124.99999999999997,
        "largeSolidVolume": 7875.000000000002
      }
    },
    "comparison": {
      "equal": true,
      "differences": []
    },
    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantity on both sides: done, solid count, total volume and the volumes of the smallest and the largest solid of the 20 mm cube (-10..10) split by the 10 mm tool cube at (5,5,5), which overlaps the cube's corner in a 5 x 5 x 5 block: two solids, the 125 block and the 7875 remainder. Bridge: Shape.split(tools:) non-nil (OCCTBooleanSplitMulti), subShapes(ofType: .solid).count, Shape.volume of the result and of each solid; the test asserts the solid count and the two solid volumes within 1e-6 (it asserted only non-nil before). Kernel: BRepAlgoAPI_Splitter with one argument and one tool, IsDone, TopExp::MapShapes solid count, BRepGProp::VolumeProperties of the result and of each TopExp_Explorer solid; the splitMulti line of the transcript at %.17g. Doubles are compared to 1e-9 relative.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-modeling-boolean-expansion/probe-evidence-fix.mm (transcript-evidence-fix.txt)"
  },
  {
    "test_name": "v0.115.0 - Boolean Expansion::cutWithHistory",
    "bridge_function": "OCCTBooleanCutWithHistory",
    "bridge_output": {
      "type": "value",
      "data": {
        "overlap": {
          "done": true,
          "valid": true,
          "volume": 7875.000000000002,
          "hasDeleted": true,
          "hasModified": true,
          "hasGenerated": true
        },
        "clear": {
          "done": true,
          "valid": true,
          "volume": 7999.999999999998,
          "hasDeleted": true,
          "hasModified": false,
          "hasGenerated": false
        },
        "buried": {
          "done": true,
          "valid": true,
          "volume": 7935.999999999996,
          "hasDeleted": true,
          "hasModified": true,
          "hasGenerated": false
        }
      }
    },
    "kernel_output": {
      "type": "value",
      "data": {
        "overlap": {
          "done": true,
          "valid": true,
          "volume": 7875.000000000002,
          "hasDeleted": true,
          "hasModified": true,
          "hasGenerated": true
        },
        "clear": {
          "done": true,
          "valid": true,
          "volume": 7999.999999999998,
          "hasDeleted": true,
          "hasModified": false,
          "hasGenerated": false
        },
        "buried": {
          "done": true,
          "valid": true,
          "volume": 7935.999999999996,
          "hasDeleted": true,
          "hasModified": true,
          "hasGenerated": false
        }
      }
    },
    "comparison": {
      "equal": true,
      "differences": []
    },
    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantity on both sides: done, valid, volume and the three history flags of the 20 mm cube (-10..10) cut by three tool cubes: overlap (10 mm at (5,5,5): deleted, modified and generated), clear (10 mm at (100,0,0): the tool is deleted, nothing of the cube is modified or generated) and buried (4 mm at (-2,-2,-2): the cube's faces are modified, none is generated). The one fixture the test used before is the overlap, which sets all three flags, so a bridge that reported true for everything passed it; the test now asserts every flag on all three tools, each on freshly built boxes. Bridge: Shape.subtractedWithHistory non-nil (OCCTBooleanCutWithHistory), shape.isValid, shape.volume, hasDeleted, hasModified, hasGenerated. Kernel: BRepAlgoAPI_Cut with SetArguments/SetTools and Build, IsDone, BRepCheck_Analyzer, BRepGProp, HasDeleted, HasModified, HasGenerated; the three cutWithHistory lines of the transcript at %.17g. Doubles are compared to 1e-9 relative.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-modeling-boolean-expansion/probe-evidence-fix.mm (transcript-evidence-fix.txt)"
  },
